[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6009640296","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69#issuecomment-6009640296","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69","id":6009640296,"node_id":"IC_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABZjPVaA","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T04:57:53Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T04:57:53Z","body":"[A10] **Mark II note** (parent [re-assessment](https://github.com/kebag-logic/milan-fpga/issues/415#issuecomment-6009637220)). ADP moves to the core in the Mark II default. The redundancy seam must exist in both placements: parent #665 keys ADP state per AVB interface, and the mailbox contract carries the interface index. The fabric part of this ticket stays valid for the all-fabric build.\n","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6009640296/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6010216843","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69#issuecomment-6010216843","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69","id":6010216843,"node_id":"IC_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABZjyhiw","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T05:48:10Z","updated_at":"2026-10-06T05:48:10Z","body":"[A10] **Lane for #69: the redundancy seam in the fabric build.** Executor [A550], branch `pp69-if-seam` from `main` `e6a759de`. Reviewers [R512] (internal) and [R513] (external).\n\nThe owner's standing rule is to keep the redundancy path open. So the seam is threaded through, not closed by decision.\n\n**Items:**\n1. **Top parameter.** `protocol_processor_top` exposes the interface count (F01.5 P-N-AVB-INTERFACES, default 1).\n   - It passes the count to `KL_adp_engine`, replacing the literal at `:1569`.\n   - It drives `rx_if_index_i` from the received frame's interface when the count is above 1, replacing the hardwired `2'd0` at `:1329`.\n   - Add an interface-index input port only at the top, defaulting to 0. The parent wiring stays unchanged at count 1.\n2. **Registry port field.** When the count is above 1, `KL_aecp_notify` stores the port per registry row (the Milan v1.2 5.3.4.2 tuple: entity_id, MAC and port). At count 1, the field is not generated.\n3. **Counters.** Say which counters are keyed per interface and which are not. Key the AVB_INTERFACE counters per interface when the count is above 1. Anything deliberately unkeyed is named with its reason.\n4. **No change at count 1.**\n   - The Yosys statistics of `protocol_processor_top` and of every touched module must be byte-identical at base and head for the shipping shape.\n   - Every suite record must be identical.\n   - Report the OOC 1x1 delta with #638's recipe, Vivado under `flock $VIVADO_LOCK`. It must be 0 LUT and 0 FF; STOP otherwise.\n5. **Elaborate at two interfaces.**\n   - A suite builds `KL_adp_engine` at N_IF_P = 2 and grades per-interface advertising.\n   - A lint-only (or suite) elaboration builds `protocol_processor_top` at count 2.\n   - A planted mutant that collapses the interface index must fail.\n6. **Docs.** The banner at `KL_aecp_notify.sv:17-20`, 01 section 7, and the REQ-SCP-003 Arch cell name what is and is not keyed.\n7. **Before any RTL edit,** run `git grep -F` for every changed line across `tb/**/*.patch` and the exact-text mutant tables. Show every arm still plants.\n\n**Gates:**\n- every processor suite and campaign;\n- `make check`, Yosys and lint;\n- the parent consumer set of 17 at parent dev `28f9666f`, with the 148 patch only (in your output directory). Add a parent patch only if the parent's wiring needs one; at count 1 it should not.\n\n**Output:** HANDOFF.md and PR-BODY.md (\"Closes #69\" if every acceptance item is met). Then post REVIEW READY with the head on #69. Do not push.\n\nDo not edit or delete any existing comment.\n","author_association":"OWNER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6010216843/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/comments/6010222994","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69#issuecomment-6010222994","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Mister-M-alt/protocol-processor-control-plane-avb-milan/issues/69","id":6010222994,"node_id":"IC_kwDOT06kyc8AAAABZjy5kg","user":{"login":"Mister-M-alt","id":161579364,"node_id":"U_kgDOCaGBZA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/161579364?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt","html_url":"https://github.com/Mister-M-alt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Mister-M-alt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-06T05:48:43Z","updated